WEBVTT

00:01.067 --> 00:03.168
[SPEAKER_00]: This is your everyday English class.

00:03.668 --> 00:04.468
[SPEAKER_00]: Hello.

00:04.848 --> 00:06.929
[SPEAKER_00]: Welcome to English Cactus.

00:07.309 --> 00:08.409
[SPEAKER_00]: My name is Anna.

00:08.889 --> 00:10.030
[SPEAKER_03]: And my name is Brian.

00:10.470 --> 00:16.592
[SPEAKER_03]: This podcast will help you practice your English in a fun and natural way, improving your listening skills.

00:17.343 --> 00:21.724
[SPEAKER_00]: Learning English in real life situations can feel difficult sometimes.

00:22.365 --> 00:30.447
[SPEAKER_00]: Maybe you understand a grammar, maybe you know many words, but when you hear a real conversation, it can still feel confusing.

00:31.067 --> 00:32.228
[SPEAKER_03]: And here's something interesting.

00:32.788 --> 00:40.070
[SPEAKER_03]: Many students study English for years, but they still feel nervous in simple everyday situations, like shopping.

00:40.712 --> 00:47.335
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, imagine you want to buy something, maybe clothes, headphones, or even a laptop.

00:47.875 --> 00:51.577
[SPEAKER_00]: Should you buy it online or should you go to a physical store?

00:52.157 --> 00:59.380
[SPEAKER_03]: Today's episode is about online shopping versus shopping in stores, a topic that is part of our daily lives.

01:00.000 --> 01:08.044
[SPEAKER_03]: In this episode, you will listen to a natural conversation where people talk about the advantages and disadvantages of both options.

01:08.926 --> 01:12.469
[SPEAKER_00]: Don't worry if you don't understand everything the first time.

01:12.669 --> 01:18.214
[SPEAKER_00]: Just relax, grab your coffee, listen carefully and enjoy the conversation.

01:18.894 --> 01:25.520
[SPEAKER_03]: After the dialogue, we will explain the most important phrases, useful vocabulary and some cultural tips.

01:26.000 --> 01:28.763
[SPEAKER_03]: This will make everything much easier to understand.

01:29.627 --> 01:32.349
[SPEAKER_00]: And don't forget to subscribe to the channel.

01:32.770 --> 01:35.032
[SPEAKER_00]: Your support is very important for us.

01:35.472 --> 01:38.314
[SPEAKER_00]: And when you subscribe, you won't miss the next lessons.

01:39.015 --> 01:41.557
[SPEAKER_03]: Also, tell us in the comments, where are you from?

01:41.957 --> 01:44.840
[SPEAKER_03]: We love seeing students from all around the world.

01:45.560 --> 01:46.982
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, grab your coffee.

01:47.482 --> 01:48.103
[SPEAKER_00]: Relax.

01:48.703 --> 01:49.504
[SPEAKER_00]: And let's begin.

01:53.633 --> 01:55.154
[SPEAKER_03]: Hey Maya, good to see you.

01:55.174 --> 01:57.276
[SPEAKER_03]: I just came back from the mall.

01:57.556 --> 01:59.678
[SPEAKER_03]: I was looking for a new pair of headphones.

02:00.459 --> 02:00.999
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh really?

02:01.159 --> 02:02.080
[SPEAKER_01]: You went to the mall?

02:02.100 --> 02:04.502
[SPEAKER_01]: I usually buy things online these days.

02:04.722 --> 02:06.123
[SPEAKER_01]: It's so much easier for me.

02:06.784 --> 02:10.187
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, I know a lot of people prefer online shopping now.

02:10.607 --> 02:13.329
[SPEAKER_03]: But honestly, I still like going to stores.

02:13.830 --> 02:16.172
[SPEAKER_03]: I like to see the product with my own eyes.

02:16.927 --> 02:17.627
[SPEAKER_01]: That makes sense.

02:18.227 --> 02:22.129
[SPEAKER_01]: When you shop online, you can't really touch the product or try it.

02:22.589 --> 02:25.010
[SPEAKER_01]: But for me, the convenience is amazing.

02:25.290 --> 02:27.111
[SPEAKER_01]: I can buy something while sitting on my couch.

02:27.811 --> 02:28.131
[SPEAKER_03]: True.

02:28.651 --> 02:31.052
[SPEAKER_03]: Online shopping is definitely convenient.

02:31.532 --> 02:34.053
[SPEAKER_03]: Last week, I ordered a phone case online.

02:34.293 --> 02:35.593
[SPEAKER_03]: It took only two minutes.

02:36.114 --> 02:38.995
[SPEAKER_03]: But when it arrived, it looked different from the pictures.

02:39.795 --> 02:40.435
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, no.

02:40.735 --> 02:41.756
[SPEAKER_01]: That happens sometimes.

02:42.196 --> 02:42.896
[SPEAKER_01]: Did you return it?

02:43.596 --> 02:46.238
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, but the return process took a while.

02:46.799 --> 02:51.023
[SPEAKER_03]: I had to print a label, go to the post office, and wait for the refund.

02:51.683 --> 02:54.206
[SPEAKER_01]: That's one thing I don't like about online shopping.

02:54.486 --> 02:56.208
[SPEAKER_01]: Returning items can be annoying.

02:56.768 --> 02:59.270
[SPEAKER_01]: In a physical store, you can just talk to the cashier.

03:00.011 --> 03:00.632
[SPEAKER_03]: Exactly.

03:01.012 --> 03:04.956
[SPEAKER_03]: Today at the store, I asked the salesperson, what do you recommend?

03:05.356 --> 03:07.458
[SPEAKER_03]: And he showed me three different headphones.

03:08.126 --> 03:09.566
[SPEAKER_01]: That's actually really helpful.

03:10.006 --> 03:13.547
[SPEAKER_01]: Sometimes I feel lost online because there are too many options.

03:14.267 --> 03:17.548
[SPEAKER_03]: Yes, on the website you see hundreds of products.

03:17.988 --> 03:19.989
[SPEAKER_03]: I keep scrolling and scrolling.

03:20.769 --> 03:21.249
[SPEAKER_01]: Same here.

03:21.449 --> 03:25.090
[SPEAKER_01]: Sometimes I spend an hour comparing prices and reading reviews.

03:25.870 --> 03:27.191
[SPEAKER_03]: Reviews are useful though.

03:27.651 --> 03:30.791
[SPEAKER_03]: I always check the reviews before buying something online.

03:31.572 --> 03:32.012
[SPEAKER_01]: Me too.

03:32.292 --> 03:36.593
[SPEAKER_01]: If I see a product with many good reviews, I feel more confident about buying it.

03:37.215 --> 03:39.856
[SPEAKER_03]: By the way, did you ever buy clothes online?

03:40.516 --> 03:41.617
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh yes, many times.

03:42.037 --> 03:43.938
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's always a little risky.

03:44.658 --> 03:45.358
[SPEAKER_01]: Why risky?

03:46.058 --> 03:47.639
[SPEAKER_01]: Because sizes are different.

03:48.039 --> 03:52.181
[SPEAKER_01]: Sometimes I order a medium, but when the package arrives, it feels like a small.

03:52.901 --> 03:54.662
[SPEAKER_03]: I know exactly what you mean.

03:55.122 --> 03:57.503
[SPEAKER_03]: Last month I ordered a jacket online.

03:57.883 --> 04:01.804
[SPEAKER_03]: It looked great in the photos, but when I tried it on, it was too tight.

04:02.485 --> 04:03.205
[SPEAKER_01]: Did you return it?

04:03.901 --> 04:06.483
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, but the return process was slow.

04:06.963 --> 04:09.485
[SPEAKER_03]: That's why I prefer buying clothes in stores.

04:09.785 --> 04:10.706
[SPEAKER_03]: I can try them on.

04:11.407 --> 04:13.328
[SPEAKER_01]: That's a big advantage of physical stores.

04:13.628 --> 04:17.091
[SPEAKER_01]: You can check the size, the material, and the color in real life.

04:17.851 --> 04:18.452
[SPEAKER_03]: Exactly.

04:18.832 --> 04:21.534
[SPEAKER_03]: Today I tried on three pairs of headphones.

04:22.055 --> 04:26.618
[SPEAKER_03]: One was too heavy, one was uncomfortable, and the last one was perfect.

04:27.338 --> 04:27.719
[SPEAKER_03]: Nice.

04:27.979 --> 04:28.940
[SPEAKER_03]: Which one did you choose?

04:29.700 --> 04:31.261
[SPEAKER_03]: The black wireless one.

04:31.602 --> 04:33.363
[SPEAKER_03]: The sound quality is amazing.

04:34.113 --> 04:34.793
[SPEAKER_03]: Sounds great.

04:35.073 --> 04:35.713
[SPEAKER_03]: How much was it?

04:36.353 --> 04:36.573
[SPEAKER_03]: It was $80.

04:36.833 --> 04:38.814
[SPEAKER_03]: That's not bad.

04:39.134 --> 04:40.394
[SPEAKER_01]: Did the store have a discount?

04:41.134 --> 04:41.934
[SPEAKER_03]: Actually, yes.

04:42.374 --> 04:47.135
[SPEAKER_03]: The original price was $100, but they had a 20% discount today.

04:47.835 --> 04:49.056
[SPEAKER_01]: Wow, that's a good deal.

04:49.576 --> 04:52.236
[SPEAKER_01]: Sometimes online stores also have big discounts.

04:52.916 --> 04:56.877
[SPEAKER_03]: That's true, especially during big sales like Black Friday.

04:57.737 --> 04:59.657
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh yes, I love Black Friday.

05:00.097 --> 05:03.378
[SPEAKER_01]: Last year, I bought a laptop online with a huge discount.

05:04.091 --> 05:06.512
[SPEAKER_03]: Did you research the product before buying it?

05:07.193 --> 05:07.713
[SPEAKER_01]: Of course.

05:08.013 --> 05:12.836
[SPEAKER_01]: I watched review videos, read customer comments, and compared prices on different websites.

05:13.516 --> 05:14.176
[SPEAKER_03]: That's smart.

05:14.617 --> 05:18.319
[SPEAKER_03]: When I shop online, I also compare prices on different sites.

05:18.839 --> 05:21.761
[SPEAKER_03]: Sometimes the same product is cheaper somewhere else.

05:22.501 --> 05:25.222
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly, and sometimes you can get free shipping.

05:25.943 --> 05:27.604
[SPEAKER_03]: Free shipping is the best.

05:28.144 --> 05:29.805
[SPEAKER_03]: Nobody likes paying for delivery.

05:30.531 --> 05:31.251
[SPEAKER_01]: Totally agree.

05:31.671 --> 05:34.032
[SPEAKER_01]: But sometimes the delivery takes too long.

05:34.672 --> 05:36.753
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, waiting can be frustrating.

05:37.213 --> 05:40.214
[SPEAKER_03]: When you buy something in a store, you take it home immediately.

05:40.914 --> 05:41.574
[SPEAKER_01]: That's true.

05:41.974 --> 05:43.274
[SPEAKER_01]: Instant satisfaction.

05:43.955 --> 05:47.376
[SPEAKER_03]: Another thing I like about physical stores is asking questions.

05:47.876 --> 05:52.897
[SPEAKER_03]: Today I asked the salesperson, sorry, did you say this model has noise canceling?

05:53.617 --> 05:54.497
[SPEAKER_03]: And what did he say?

05:55.138 --> 05:56.638
[SPEAKER_03]: He said, yes, it does.

05:57.018 --> 05:58.799
[SPEAKER_03]: And the battery lasts about 30 hours.

06:00.227 --> 06:00.967
[SPEAKER_03]: That's impressive.

06:01.628 --> 06:05.010
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, and I could test the headphones right there in the store.

06:05.710 --> 06:07.471
[SPEAKER_03]: That's something you can't do online.

06:08.191 --> 06:08.792
[SPEAKER_03]: Exactly.

06:09.172 --> 06:12.033
[SPEAKER_03]: But online shopping still has many advantages.

06:12.734 --> 06:13.154
[SPEAKER_03]: Like what?

06:13.834 --> 06:16.836
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, you can shop anytime, even at midnight.

06:17.576 --> 06:18.817
[SPEAKER_01]: That's my favorite part.

06:19.177 --> 06:22.739
[SPEAKER_01]: Last night, I bought a book at 11.30 p.m. See?

06:23.199 --> 06:24.840
[SPEAKER_03]: Stores were probably closed.

06:25.520 --> 06:26.081
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

06:26.421 --> 06:27.982
[SPEAKER_01]: Online stores never close.

06:28.688 --> 06:30.210
[SPEAKER_03]: Another thing is variety.

06:30.810 --> 06:33.212
[SPEAKER_03]: Online stores usually have more options.

06:33.993 --> 06:37.497
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, sometimes local stores don't have the product you want.

06:38.177 --> 06:40.780
[SPEAKER_03]: True, but sometimes the opposite happens.

06:41.180 --> 06:44.103
[SPEAKER_03]: A store may have a product that is sold out online.

06:44.804 --> 06:45.885
[SPEAKER_03]: That's also true.

06:46.525 --> 06:49.949
[SPEAKER_03]: I guess both options have advantages and disadvantages.

06:50.709 --> 06:52.972
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, it really depends on what you're buying.

06:53.711 --> 06:58.534
[SPEAKER_03]: For example, electronics can be good online because you can compare many models.

06:59.295 --> 07:02.617
[SPEAKER_01]: But clothes and shoes are easier in physical stores.

07:03.377 --> 07:03.978
[SPEAKER_03]: Exactly.

07:04.598 --> 07:07.920
[SPEAKER_03]: By the way, do you prefer paying online or in person?

07:08.661 --> 07:09.401
[SPEAKER_01]: Good question.

07:09.801 --> 07:14.144
[SPEAKER_01]: Online payments are easy, but sometimes I feel safer paying in the store.

07:14.805 --> 07:15.445
[SPEAKER_03]: I understand.

07:15.765 --> 07:18.207
[SPEAKER_03]: Some people worry about online security.

07:18.907 --> 07:22.990
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, I always check if the website is safe before entering my credit card.

07:23.644 --> 07:25.024
[SPEAKER_03]: That's a very good habit.

07:25.584 --> 07:26.205
[SPEAKER_03]: What about you?

07:26.225 --> 07:28.765
[SPEAKER_03]: Do you use your phone to pay online?

07:29.405 --> 07:31.326
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, sometimes it's very quick.

07:31.566 --> 07:33.666
[SPEAKER_01]: Just a few clicks and the order is done.

07:34.346 --> 07:36.927
[SPEAKER_03]: Technology really changed the way we shop.

07:37.607 --> 07:38.347
[SPEAKER_01]: Definitely.

07:39.087 --> 07:41.848
[SPEAKER_01]: 20 years ago, online shopping was not very common.

07:42.528 --> 07:44.608
[SPEAKER_03]: Now it's part of our daily lives.

07:45.289 --> 07:51.730
[SPEAKER_01]: But I still enjoy visiting stores sometimes, walking around, seeing new products, and maybe finding a surprise.

07:52.543 --> 07:53.083
[SPEAKER_03]: Same here.

07:53.564 --> 07:56.765
[SPEAKER_03]: Sometimes shopping in stores is also a social activity.

07:57.525 --> 07:58.246
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

07:58.486 --> 07:59.766
[SPEAKER_01]: You can go shopping with friends.

08:00.527 --> 08:02.188
[SPEAKER_03]: And maybe grab a coffee after.

08:02.888 --> 08:03.888
[SPEAKER_03]: That sounds perfect.

08:04.569 --> 08:05.789
[SPEAKER_03]: So, what do you think?

08:06.290 --> 08:08.531
[SPEAKER_03]: Online shopping or shopping in stores?

08:09.211 --> 08:10.572
[SPEAKER_01]: Honestly, I like both.

08:11.012 --> 08:15.354
[SPEAKER_01]: Online shopping is great for convenience and stores are great for experience.

08:16.158 --> 08:16.639
[SPEAKER_03]: I agree.

08:16.979 --> 08:19.802
[SPEAKER_03]: The best option is using both when it makes sense.

08:20.603 --> 08:21.183
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

08:21.464 --> 08:22.305
[SPEAKER_01]: Smart shopping.

08:23.005 --> 08:23.586
[SPEAKER_03]: Well said.

08:24.066 --> 08:29.712
[SPEAKER_03]: And remember, keep learning, keep exploring, and keep improving your English every day.

08:30.433 --> 08:30.713
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

08:31.014 --> 08:34.898
[SPEAKER_01]: Study English every day, learn something new, and you're doing great.

08:35.158 --> 08:35.658
[SPEAKER_01]: Keep going.

08:36.279 --> 08:37.500
[SPEAKER_01]: Thanks for the chat, Maya.

08:38.141 --> 08:38.862
[SPEAKER_01]: Anytime, Lucas.

08:40.900 --> 08:45.423
[SPEAKER_00]: Wow, that was a really interesting conversation between Lucas and Maya.

08:45.903 --> 08:48.585
[SPEAKER_00]: They talked about something that is part of our daily life.

08:49.145 --> 08:49.586
[SPEAKER_00]: Shopping.

08:50.206 --> 08:52.528
[SPEAKER_00]: Online shopping and shopping in stores.

08:53.068 --> 08:56.230
[SPEAKER_02]: Don't worry if you didn't understand everything in the conversation.

08:56.510 --> 08:57.651
[SPEAKER_02]: That's completely normal.

08:58.131 --> 09:01.974
[SPEAKER_02]: Now we will go step by step and it will become much easier.

09:02.615 --> 09:05.836
[SPEAKER_00]: Let's begin with some important phrases from the dialogue.

09:06.577 --> 09:11.459
[SPEAKER_00]: Lucas said the sentence, I like to see the product with my own eyes.

09:12.139 --> 09:14.700
[SPEAKER_00]: This sentence is very natural in English.

09:15.260 --> 09:20.642
[SPEAKER_00]: Lucas is explaining that he prefers shopping in stores because he can look at the product directly.

09:21.343 --> 09:26.885
[SPEAKER_00]: When we say with my own eyes, we mean we want to personally see something to be sure.

09:27.685 --> 09:32.167
[SPEAKER_00]: For example, you might say, That's a great phrase because it shows trust and personal verification.

09:32.187 --> 09:36.249
[SPEAKER_00]: When Lucas says this, he means that pictures online are sometimes not enough.

09:49.335 --> 09:55.477
[SPEAKER_02]: Now, Maya answered with a very common idea when she said, I can buy something while sitting on my couch.

09:56.098 --> 09:57.758
[SPEAKER_02]: This sentence shows convenience.

09:58.178 --> 10:00.139
[SPEAKER_02]: It means you don't need to leave your house.

10:00.439 --> 10:02.980
[SPEAKER_02]: You can buy products from your phone or computer.

10:03.480 --> 10:06.902
[SPEAKER_02]: You could also say, I ordered dinner while sitting on my couch.

10:07.522 --> 10:10.543
[SPEAKER_02]: Or, I bought my shoes online while sitting at home.

10:11.143 --> 10:11.864
[SPEAKER_00]: Let's continue.

10:12.525 --> 10:15.107
[SPEAKER_00]: Lucas later said, Did you return it?

10:15.668 --> 10:18.831
[SPEAKER_00]: This is a very practical question when talking about shopping.

10:19.532 --> 10:24.557
[SPEAKER_00]: Return means giving the product back to the store because you are not satisfied.

10:25.178 --> 10:28.842
[SPEAKER_00]: You might say, I returned the shirt because it was too small.

10:29.462 --> 10:32.826
[SPEAKER_00]: Or, I returned the phone because it didn't work well.

10:33.392 --> 10:36.735
[SPEAKER_02]: And Lucas also asked a common shopping question in the store.

10:37.256 --> 10:38.177
[SPEAKER_02]: What do you recommend?

10:38.677 --> 10:41.540
[SPEAKER_02]: This is extremely useful when you don't know what to choose.

10:42.041 --> 10:43.742
[SPEAKER_02]: You can use it in many situations.

10:44.183 --> 10:46.305
[SPEAKER_02]: In a restaurant, what do you recommend?

10:46.805 --> 10:49.688
[SPEAKER_02]: In a clothing store, what do you recommend for winter?

10:50.249 --> 10:53.472
[SPEAKER_02]: In an electronics store, what laptop do you recommend?

10:54.088 --> 11:01.031
[SPEAKER_00]: Another natural phrase from the dialogue was when Lucas asked, sorry, did you say this model has noise canceling?

11:01.671 --> 11:04.313
[SPEAKER_00]: This is a polite way to confirm information.

11:04.813 --> 11:07.734
[SPEAKER_00]: Sometimes we didn't hear correctly, so we ask again.

11:08.334 --> 11:12.016
[SPEAKER_00]: You can say, sorry, did you say large or medium?

11:12.576 --> 11:15.338
[SPEAKER_00]: Or, sorry, did you say the meeting is at 3 p.m.?

11:16.650 --> 11:20.352
[SPEAKER_02]: Another great phrase appeared when Maya talked about online shopping.

11:20.793 --> 11:23.534
[SPEAKER_02]: She said, I feel more confident about buying it.

11:24.155 --> 11:28.358
[SPEAKER_02]: Feel confident means you feel sure or comfortable about your decision.

11:28.778 --> 11:33.441
[SPEAKER_02]: For example, I feel confident about this product because it has many good reviews.

11:34.001 --> 11:36.603
[SPEAKER_02]: Or, I feel confident speaking English now.

11:37.200 --> 11:40.264
[SPEAKER_00]: And finally, Lucas said something very interesting.

11:40.904 --> 11:43.808
[SPEAKER_00]: Technology really changed the way we shop.

11:44.468 --> 11:46.871
[SPEAKER_00]: This sentence talks about transformation.

11:47.372 --> 11:49.454
[SPEAKER_00]: Technology has changed our habits.

11:50.035 --> 11:58.104
[SPEAKER_00]: You could say similar sentences like technology changed the way we communicate, or the internet changed the way we learn.

11:58.803 --> 12:01.344
[SPEAKER_02]: As you can see, these sentences are very practical.

12:01.604 --> 12:05.626
[SPEAKER_02]: You can use them in real life when shopping, traveling, or talking with friends.

12:06.266 --> 12:10.528
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, let's talk about some important vocabulary that appeared in the dialogue.

12:11.048 --> 12:15.390
[SPEAKER_00]: These words are extremely useful if you want to talk about shopping in English.

12:16.283 --> 12:18.625
[SPEAKER_00]: The first word is convenience.

12:19.146 --> 12:23.309
[SPEAKER_00]: Convenience means something is easy and saves time or effort.

12:24.010 --> 12:29.355
[SPEAKER_00]: Maya said that online shopping is convenient because she can buy things without leaving home.

12:30.015 --> 12:37.121
[SPEAKER_00]: For example, online banking is very convenient, or living close to work is convenient.

12:37.762 --> 12:43.347
[SPEAKER_00]: The opposite idea could be inconvenient, which means something causes difficulty or trouble.

12:43.924 --> 12:45.765
[SPEAKER_02]: The second word is return.

12:46.245 --> 12:50.286
[SPEAKER_02]: To return means to give a product back to the store after buying it.

12:50.826 --> 12:53.867
[SPEAKER_02]: People usually return products for several reasons.

12:54.267 --> 12:59.789
[SPEAKER_02]: Maybe the size is wrong, maybe the item is damaged, or maybe they simply change their mind.

13:00.189 --> 13:04.150
[SPEAKER_02]: For example, I need to return these shoes because they are too small.

13:04.730 --> 13:07.671
[SPEAKER_02]: Or, the store has a 30-day return policy.

13:08.433 --> 13:14.576
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, let's talk about some cultural aspects of shopping, especially in countries like the United States.

13:15.356 --> 13:17.657
[SPEAKER_00]: One interesting thing is return policies.

13:18.298 --> 13:22.920
[SPEAKER_00]: Many stores allow customers to return products within a certain number of days.

13:23.398 --> 13:27.463
[SPEAKER_02]: Yes, and in many American stores you can return items within 30 days.

13:27.924 --> 13:30.026
[SPEAKER_02]: Sometimes you even receive a full refund.

13:30.467 --> 13:32.569
[SPEAKER_02]: However, you usually need the receipt.

13:32.990 --> 13:36.474
[SPEAKER_02]: The receipt is the paper or digital proof of your purchase.

13:36.954 --> 13:39.477
[SPEAKER_00]: Another cultural point is customer service.

13:40.138 --> 13:46.722
[SPEAKER_00]: In many physical stores in the United States, salespeople will approach you and ask, can I help you find something?

13:47.043 --> 13:51.005
[SPEAKER_02]: If you want help, you can say, yes, I'm looking for headphones.

13:51.566 --> 13:57.009
[SPEAKER_02]: But if you prefer to look around alone, you can politely say, no thanks, I'm just looking.

13:57.409 --> 14:00.511
[SPEAKER_00]: Another interesting difference is about price comparison.

14:01.112 --> 14:06.215
[SPEAKER_00]: Many people in the US check prices online even while they are inside a store.

14:06.756 --> 14:08.677
[SPEAKER_00]: They compare prices using their phones.

14:09.086 --> 14:11.587
[SPEAKER_02]: This behavior is sometimes called showrooming.

14:11.987 --> 14:16.830
[SPEAKER_02]: People look at the product in the store, but they buy it online if the price is cheaper.

14:17.270 --> 14:18.731
[SPEAKER_00]: But stores are adapting.

14:19.191 --> 14:21.212
[SPEAKER_00]: Some stores now offer price matching.

14:21.592 --> 14:26.034
[SPEAKER_02]: Price matching means the store will match the online price, so you can buy it there.

14:26.474 --> 14:29.196
[SPEAKER_00]: Another cultural aspect is Black Friday.

14:29.516 --> 14:33.358
[SPEAKER_02]: Black Friday is one of the biggest shopping days in the United States.

14:33.658 --> 14:35.459
[SPEAKER_02]: It happens the day after Thanksgiving.

14:35.987 --> 14:41.328
[SPEAKER_00]: Stores offer huge discounts, and many people wake up very early to go shopping.

14:41.648 --> 14:45.009
[SPEAKER_02]: And nowadays, many of those deals are also available online.

14:45.429 --> 14:48.629
[SPEAKER_00]: Shopping culture continues to change because of technology.

14:49.030 --> 14:54.090
[SPEAKER_00]: But one thing remains the same, people always look for good quality and good prices.

14:54.471 --> 14:54.991
[SPEAKER_02]: Exactly.

14:55.471 --> 15:01.752
[SPEAKER_02]: And learning how to talk about these situations in English helps you feel more confident when traveling or shopping abroad.

15:02.204 --> 15:08.407
[SPEAKER_00]: Now that we understand the dialogue, the vocabulary, and the cultural tips, let's help you practice a little more.

15:08.688 --> 15:14.010
[SPEAKER_02]: Yes, in this part we will show you simple sentence models you can use when talking about shopping.

15:14.451 --> 15:18.513
[SPEAKER_02]: These sentences are very practical, and you can adapt them to many situations.

15:18.953 --> 15:20.094
[SPEAKER_00]: The idea is simple.

15:20.414 --> 15:24.116
[SPEAKER_00]: You learn a structure, and then you change a few words to create your own sentence.

15:24.467 --> 15:26.888
[SPEAKER_02]: Don't worry if you feel nervous speaking English.

15:27.108 --> 15:27.708
[SPEAKER_02]: That's normal.

15:28.048 --> 15:29.509
[SPEAKER_02]: Start with simple sentences.

15:29.949 --> 15:32.290
[SPEAKER_02]: Step by step, you will feel more confident.

15:32.650 --> 15:33.150
[SPEAKER_02]: Keep going.

15:33.330 --> 15:34.011
[SPEAKER_02]: You're doing great.

15:34.491 --> 15:37.812
[SPEAKER_00]: One very useful structure is, I'm looking for.

15:38.652 --> 15:42.054
[SPEAKER_00]: Example, I'm looking for wireless headphones.

15:42.414 --> 15:44.234
[SPEAKER_02]: You can change the product easily.

15:44.574 --> 15:47.135
[SPEAKER_02]: For example, I'm looking for a black jacket.

15:47.676 --> 15:49.256
[SPEAKER_02]: I'm looking for running shoes.

15:49.716 --> 15:51.217
[SPEAKER_02]: I'm looking for a phone charger.

15:51.605 --> 15:54.326
[SPEAKER_00]: If you forget the word, you can say something even simpler.

15:54.946 --> 15:55.846
[SPEAKER_00]: This one, please.

15:56.246 --> 15:57.747
[SPEAKER_02]: Simple English works very well.

15:58.027 --> 15:59.367
[SPEAKER_02]: Communication is the goal.

15:59.767 --> 16:03.188
[SPEAKER_02]: Another very useful sentence is, what do you recommend?

16:03.608 --> 16:06.349
[SPEAKER_00]: This sentence is extremely common in stores.

16:06.849 --> 16:09.590
[SPEAKER_00]: Example, what headphones do you recommend?

16:10.030 --> 16:12.110
[SPEAKER_02]: Or, what laptop do you recommend?

16:12.610 --> 16:14.531
[SPEAKER_02]: What shoes do you recommend for walking?

16:15.010 --> 16:18.252
[SPEAKER_00]: This question helps you start a conversation with the salesperson.

16:18.632 --> 16:22.214
[SPEAKER_00]: Another important question when shopping is, how much is this?

16:22.734 --> 16:24.295
[SPEAKER_02]: Very simple and very useful.

16:24.715 --> 16:26.856
[SPEAKER_02]: For example, how much is this jacket?

16:27.296 --> 16:28.517
[SPEAKER_02]: How much are these shoes?

16:28.917 --> 16:30.338
[SPEAKER_00]: Remember something important.

16:30.698 --> 16:34.040
[SPEAKER_00]: When the product is one item, we say how much is this.

16:34.560 --> 16:38.482
[SPEAKER_00]: When the product is more than one item, we say how much are these?

16:38.967 --> 16:41.408
[SPEAKER_02]: For example, how much are these headphones?

16:41.948 --> 16:43.429
[SPEAKER_02]: You can also ask about discounts.

16:43.969 --> 16:46.351
[SPEAKER_02]: Example, is there a discount?

16:46.371 --> 16:48.612
[SPEAKER_00]: Or you can say, is this on sale?

16:48.852 --> 16:51.113
[SPEAKER_02]: For example, is this jacket on sale?

16:51.557 --> 16:54.958
[SPEAKER_00]: Sales and discounts are very common in shopping conversations.

16:55.358 --> 16:59.779
[SPEAKER_00]: If you are talking about online shopping, you can say, I bought this online.

17:00.259 --> 17:02.120
[SPEAKER_02]: Or, I ordered this online.

17:02.540 --> 17:03.520
[SPEAKER_00]: Example sentences.

17:04.141 --> 17:05.961
[SPEAKER_00]: I ordered these shoes online.

17:06.441 --> 17:07.982
[SPEAKER_00]: I bought this phone online.

17:08.242 --> 17:10.962
[SPEAKER_02]: You can also say, the delivery was very fast.

17:11.483 --> 17:12.963
[SPEAKER_02]: Or, the shipping was free.

17:13.525 --> 17:15.646
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's the end of today's episode.

17:16.247 --> 17:23.732
[SPEAKER_00]: Today we talked about online shopping and shopping in stores, two very common experiences in our daily lives.

17:24.452 --> 17:25.113
[SPEAKER_02]: Exactly.

17:25.593 --> 17:37.221
[SPEAKER_02]: You learned useful phrases for shopping, important vocabulary like discount, return, shipping and review, and also some cultural tips about how people shop in different places.

17:38.048 --> 17:40.610
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, here's the most important part.

17:41.111 --> 17:41.851
[SPEAKER_00]: Practice.

17:42.412 --> 17:44.633
[SPEAKER_00]: Try to use these phrases in your daily life.

17:45.154 --> 17:51.819
[SPEAKER_00]: When you visit a store, try asking simple questions like, how much is this, or what do you recommend?

17:52.580 --> 18:00.306
[SPEAKER_02]: And when you shop online, try reading reviews in English, comparing prices, and paying attention to the vocabulary you learned today.

18:01.127 --> 18:04.830
[SPEAKER_00]: Small actions like these help you improve your English naturally.

18:05.498 --> 18:08.699
[SPEAKER_02]: Do you prefer shopping online or shopping in stores?

18:09.439 --> 18:11.020
[SPEAKER_00]: Why do you prefer that option?

18:11.680 --> 18:12.640
[SPEAKER_02]: Tell us in the comments.

18:13.100 --> 18:15.741
[SPEAKER_02]: Your answer can help other students practice English too.

18:16.421 --> 18:19.022
[SPEAKER_00]: And remember, learning English is a journey.

18:19.462 --> 18:20.802
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't need to be perfect.

18:21.022 --> 18:23.463
[SPEAKER_00]: Just keep practicing a little every day.

18:24.203 --> 18:28.144
[SPEAKER_02]: Study English every day, learn something new, and don't give up.

18:28.785 --> 18:29.685
[SPEAKER_00]: You're doing great!

18:30.415 --> 18:36.681
[SPEAKER_02]: If you enjoyed this episode, subscribe to the channel and share this podcast with a friend who is also learning English.

18:37.402 --> 18:40.445
[SPEAKER_00]: The more you listen, the more confident you will become.

18:41.125 --> 18:41.906
[SPEAKER_00]: Keep practicing.

18:42.507 --> 18:43.287
[SPEAKER_00]: Keep improving.

18:43.888 --> 18:44.549
[SPEAKER_02]: And take care.

